  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe docs now say which \"mill-turn\" they mean. CamCraft's Mill-turn kind is a lathe with live tooling. Turning on a mill (the part in the mill spindle, lathe tools on the table, one work offset for each tool) is a different setup. CamCraft does not support it yet (#2580).\n\n- A box with the two meanings:\n  - `site/content/guide/operations/operations-turning.md`, after the introduction.\n  - `site/content/guide/check-and-post/machines.md`, at the start of the Mill-turn section.\n- `site/content/guide/reference/glossary.md`: the Mill-turn entry names the live-tooling kind and `millturn.mch`. A new entry, \"Turning on a mill\", describes the other setup.\n- `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`: the `load_machine` row names the `\"Mill-turn\"` preset and the two meanings. It tells an agent to confirm which one a user means.\n- Each other bare \"mill-turn\" in the guide and in `README.md` now says \"(live tooling)\" or \"(a lathe with live tooling)\". The `.mch` kind values (`mill`, `lathe`, `mill-turn`) and the UI kind filter list stay as they are, because they are literal values.\n- `docs/decisions/2581-mill-turn-glossary.md` records the choice of terms.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `zola build` (Zola 0.23.6, the version pinned in `release.yml`): 47 pages, no errors. The new link to `machines.md#mill-turn` resolves.\n- `ZOLA=<zola> python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests`: 62 tests, 2 failed. The two failures are `test_component_static_icons_and_license_match_app` (`site/static/icons/act-report.png` is missing). They fail on `upstream/main` without this change too.\n- Search: `grep -rniI \"mill-turn\" site/content README.md` finds no use that leaves the meaning open.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nNone: docs-only change.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No Rust build or gate: the change touches no code.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #2581\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
